# SUPERSEDED by upstream implementation PR #166495

This artifact captured the original consumer fix for issue #166466 and was useful for establishing the
bug shape. It is no longer the preferred implementation reference.

Upstream PR #166495 (`02c316342775562101fc980b3728fab24e871c3e`) closes #166466 with a broader and
stronger owner-level repair:

- shared `hasPendingUpdateRecoverySeal()` / `assertUpdateRecoverySealComplete()` classifier;
- discovery treats retained partial manifests as incomplete evidence;
- baseline reuse refuses incomplete publication;
- forward-resolution metadata access checks seal completion before and after reads;
- candidate/prepared generations remain evidence without being promoted to verified rollback points;
- Doctor retirement re-checks the partial immediately before authority validation and deletion;
- duplicate OpenClaw publication ownership is removed in favor of the fs-safe 0.24.2 publisher.

Keep this file only as provenance for the earlier #166466 handoff. Do not recommend applying this
older patch over #166495.

